<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kalinjar Fort</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kalanjara</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kalinjar Fort is a hill fortress in Banda district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on the edge of the Vindhya range in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a>. One of the strongest fortresses of medieval India, it was a chief stronghold of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandela-dynasty">Chandela dynasty</a> until Qutb al-Din Aibak took it in 1203. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sher-shah-suri">Sher Shah Suri</a> died at its siege in 1545; it was later held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundela">Bundelas</a> and passed to the British in 1812.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kalinjar-fort.jpg" alt="Kalinjar Fort" width="320" height="178" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MacKenzie, Colin (1754-1821) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:E._view_of_the_Fort_at_Kalinjar._May_1814.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
